# GJS style

Match `extension.js`: ES modules, single quotes, semicolons, 4-space indent, trailing commas in multiline literals. Use `const` and `let`.

Group `gi://` imports, then `resource:///` imports, then local modules. One blank line between groups.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
const Main = imports.ui.main;

// ✅ GOOD
import GLib from 'gi://GLib';

import {Extension, gettext as _} from 'resource:///org/gnome/shell/extensions/extension.js';
import * as Main from 'resource:///org/gnome/shell/ui/main.js';

import {TopBar} from './features/topBar.js';
```

Prefix private methods and fields with `_`. Feature files are `camelCase.js`. Classes are `PascalCase`. Named exports for features and preference pages. Default export only for the `Extension` subclass in `extension.js` and the `ExtensionPreferences` subclass in `prefs.js`.

Return early from a guard. The main path stays at the top level of the function. Use a large `if` only when both branches are the work.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
if (this._clock) {
    const parent = this._clock.get_parent();
    if (parent)
        parent.remove_child(this._clock);
}

// ✅ GOOD
if (!this._clock)
    return;

const parent = this._clock.get_parent();
if (!parent)
    return;

parent.remove_child(this._clock);
```

Keep an `if` when code after it must still run. Do not comment what the next line does. Comment a shell constraint the code does not show.
